  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is encapsulation?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Encapsulation bundles data and methods within a class and restricts direct access to internal state, protecting object integrity."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Encapsulation hides internal state and requires interaction through public methods. Implemented using access modifiers (private, public, protected). Provides data validation and reduces coupling."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Encapsulation Example",
        "content": "public class BankAccount {\n    private decimal balance;\n    \n    public decimal GetBalance() => balance;\n    \n    public void Deposit(decimal amount) {\n        if (amount > 0) balance += amount;\n    }\n}",
        "language": "csharp"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Interviewer's Expectation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Interviewers assess understanding of data hiding, access modifiers, and object integrity."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Common Mistakes"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
